& [EmptyFixtureEnvironment] is caught by the first successful-cycle run
  + [observation] is the existing core correctly rejects an inspect request whose expected package set is empty
  + [cause] is the initial mock shortcut constructed an empty runtime rather than exercising a signed semantic authority
  + [repair] is compile one real SOP document with distinct deterministic test signers and bind the request to its exact package digest and declared scope
  + [security_result] is the success proof now crosses the same compilation, trust admission, request execution, and response-verification boundary as production core behavior
  + [status] is resolved

& [PackageDigestLocator] is caught while forming the signed fixture
  + [observation] is package digest belongs to the optional recognition certificate rather than PackageContent
  + [repair] is require a signed certificate and copy its digest into ExpectedPackage
  + [status] is resolved

& [RouteAdmissionGap] is found during post-success protocol review
  + [observation] is knowing both participants did not prove that their sender-recipient pair was authorized for the declared message kind
  + [risk] is a known participant could address a semantically wrong stage without leaving the commissioned participant set
  + [repair] is enforce the fixed Phase 1 role-and-identity route for every message kind and reject fault envelopes as hidden control flow
  + [proof] is wrong-route and effect-broker tests preserve the accepted prefix
  + [status] is resolved

& [ResponseContractGap] is found during post-success protocol review
  + [observation] is expected response kind and deadline were serialized but not enforced at causal handoff
  + [risk] is an accepted predecessor could be followed by the wrong stage or by a logically late response
  + [repair] is validate each declared next kind locally and require the caused message to match that kind at or before its deadline
  + [proof] is wrong-kind, absent-contract, late-response, and expiry tests
  + [status] is resolved

& [UnboundedProfileCollections] is found during machine-form audit
  + [observation] is transcript byte budgets bounded accepted serialization but commission and payload collections had no explicit profile cardinality
  + [repair] is cap each profile-owned collection at 256 items while retaining the stricter serialized-byte budget for admitted messages
  + [proof] is oversized authority and acceptance-criterion tests
  + [status] is resolved

& [EffectGrantAmbiguity] is found during authority review
  + [observation] is execution performed no effect but the initial commission validator allowed a nonempty effect-class capability
  + [risk] is a Phase 1 record could appear to grant authority that the canonical activation explicitly withholds
  + [repair] is reject every commission containing an exterior effect class before any transcript message
  + [status] is resolved

& [OutcomeCoherenceGap] is found during transport review
  + [observation] is strict JSON decoding alone did not cross-check duplicated top-level values, transcript payloads, review, decision, and metrics
  + [risk] is a syntactically valid transported outcome could contain internally rewritten claims
  + [repair] is CycleOutcome validation replays all seven messages, verifies the core response, reproduces Observer review, checks decision and progress, and recomputes metrics
  + [proof] is round-trip success plus rewritten metrics, candidate, and final-reason rejection
  + [status] is resolved

& [PriorEvidenceStaleness] is correctly caught by the first global run
  + [observation] is earlier evidence tests rejected the changed shared slice index by exact byte count before later workspace tests ran
  + [cause] is the project navigation and plan files are content-addressed by prerequisite proof manifests
  + [repair] is finish the shared project surfaces then regenerate prepared-runtime, resident-service, service-backed-MCP, and supervised-lifecycle manifests in dependency order before generating the new manifest
